 ## Overview
-Palette Compression with Reference Counting and Reuse is a memory optimization technique for dense voxel grids that maps voxel types to a compact palette of entries, storing indices into the palette rather than full type values to save memory [S1]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods in the [Compact Voxel Section Storage](4219-compact-voxel-section-storage.md) tree by specifically handling mixed-material sections through dynamic palette management with reference counting, rather than relying on static empty or uniform modes.
