 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
--   **Index Compression:** The initial implementation may forget to compress the indices. While compressing indices is optional, using plain bytes is acceptable only if the palette stays below 256 variants [S1]. If the palette exceeds 256, indices must be widened to shorts or ints, increasing memory usage [S1].
--   **Refcount Underflow:** Ensure that `refcount` is not decremented below zero. This should not happen if every `set` operation correctly decrements the old entry's refcount before incrementing the new one.
--   **Palette Growth:** When growing the palette, ensure that new entries are properly initialized (zero refcount) to avoid stale data issues [S1].
